checkDegrees -- compares the degrees of generators of two modules
*****************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        d = checkDegrees(N,M)
        d = checkDegrees(n,m)
  * Inputs:
      * N, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, 
      * n, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, presentation of N; 
      * M, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, 
      * m, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, presentation of M; 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Strict: checkDegrees_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmStrict=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value false, forces strict equality of degrees
      * Verbose => ..., default value false
  * Outputs:
      * d, a *note sequence: (Macaulay2Doc)Sequence,, (Boolean, a degree in the
        ring of M and N)

Description
===========

This is to be used with *note isIsomorphic: isIsomorphic,.

The routine compares the sorted lists of degrees of generators of the two
modules; the degreeLength (can be anything). If the numbers of generators of
M,N are different, the modules are not isomorphic, and the routine returns
(false, null).

If the numbers are the same, and all the corresponding degrees pairs differ by
the same amount (so that the modules might become isomorphic after a shift,
then if Strict => false (the default) the output (true, e) tells how to adjust
the modules to make the degrees equal: either tensor N with (ring N)^{e} or
tensor M with (ring M)^{-e}.

If Strict => true, then the output is (false, null) unless the offset e is 0.

