isomorphism -- retrieve an isomorphism of modules
*************************************************

  * Usage: 
        f = isomorphism(N, M)
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, 
      * N, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Homogeneous => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default
        value true, if false, allow an inhomogeneous isomorphism;
      * Verbose => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value
        false, whether to print debugging information;
      * Strict => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value
        false, whether to force strict equality of degrees;
      * Tries => an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value null, the
        number of attempts at generating random map;
      * Strategy (missing documentation) => ..., default value null, 
  * Outputs:
      * f, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, an isomorphism $M \to N$; 

Description
===========

This method retrieves the isomorphism between the given modules. Note that this
isomorphism is already cached if a previous call to *note isIsomorphic:
isIsomorphic, returned true, but otherwise that function is called.

